      "rev_n_3_391a7a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_391a7a_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_391a7a",
        "thought_text": "Consider replacing a number with a multiple of the GCD of all numbers.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514892.8687372
      },
      "rev_n_1_b9071b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_b9071b_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_b9071b",
        "thought_text": "Instead of trying to replace each element with every possible number, we should consider that the maximum possible GCD after a single replacement will always be a divisor of the current GCD. We can iterate through all divisors of the current GCD and check if replacing any element with a multiple of this divisor would result in a higher GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_b9071b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ad3c1f9e61",
        "created_at": 1794514910.9322858
      },
      "rev_n_2_d37c1d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_d37c1d_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_d37c1d",
        "thought_text": "Identify pairs of numbers with the same remainder when divided by the GCD of all numbers, and consider replacing one number in each pair with a multiple of the GCD to maximize the overall GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_d37c1d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0004d6fdbb",
        "created_at": 1794514937.1484976
      },
      "rev_n_3_391a7a_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_391a7a_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_391a7a",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of replacing a number with a multiple of the GCD of all numbers is not optimal. Instead, we should consider replacing a number with the GCD of all other numbers except itself. This approach ensures that we maximize the GCD while still considering all possible replacements.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_391a7a_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_81f7d799f8",
        "created_at": 1794514959.514598
      },
      "rev_n_4_654de8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_654de8_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_654de8",
        "thought_text": "Focus on finding the maximum possible GCD by considering the impact of replacing each element.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3384801160536496564",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514979.9038622
      },
      "rev_n_5_4cf2b7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_4cf2b7_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_4cf2b7",
        "thought_text": "Instead of just calculating the current GCD, consider the effect of replacing each element with its multiples to find the highest possible GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3384801160536496564",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514979.903878
      },
      "rev_n_6_e2ab4b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_e2ab4b_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_e2ab4b",
        "thought_text": "Evaluate the divisors of the current GCD and check if replacing any element with a multiple of these divisors can increase the GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3384801160536496564",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514979.9038858
      },
      "rev_n_4_654de8_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_654de8_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_654de8",
        "thought_text": "Focus on finding the maximum possible GCD by considering the impact of replacing each element. Instead of iterating through all divisors of the current GCD, we should focus on the prime factors of the current GCD and check if replacing any element with a multiple of these prime factors would result in a higher GCD. This approach can significantly reduce the number of calculations and avoid the error in the previous implementation.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3384801160536496564",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_654de8_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9d1c46c9df",
        "created_at": 1794514998.517953
      },
      "rev_n_5_4cf2b7_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_4cf2b7_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_4cf2b7",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking if replacing an element with a multiple of the divisor would result in a higher GCD, we should consider the effect of replacing each element with the divisor itself. This approach will correctly identify the maximum possible GCD after a single replacement, as any multiple of the divisor will still be divisible by the divisor.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3384801160536496564",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_4cf2b7_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_97cb1fb171",
